\ ==== pitch>midi ( pitch -- n ), pitch>hz ( pitch -- hz ),
\      note-on ( pitch velocity instrument -- ), note-off ( pitch instrument -- ),
\      render-audio ( seconds -- matrix ), silence-audio ( -- ) ====

\ A pitch is a MIDI note number in [0, 127] or a symbol: a letter a-g, an
\ optional # (sharp) or b (flat), and an octave from -1 to 9, so :c4 is 60
\ and :a4 is 69; frequencies are equal-tempered with :a4 at 440 Hz.
\ render-audio advances the synthesizer by `seconds` and answers an n x 2
\ matrix at 48 kHz, column 0 left, column 1 right; notes started or released
\ between calls take effect at the start of the next render. A note takes
\ one of 32 voices; when none is free it takes the voice released longest
\ ago, else the one started longest ago. A note-on for a pitch already
\ sounding on the instrument retriggers that voice. Each instrument plays
\ its own patch.
\ :level and velocity scale the output, velocity by :velocity-sensitivity (0
\ ignores it); :pan places the voice with a constant-power law. silence-audio
\ ends every sounding voice; the instruments keep their patches.

11 seed

: amp ( v hz -- a ) 48000 swap amplitude-at 1000 * round 1000 / ;
: left ( stereo -- v ) | stereo | stereo 0 stereo n-rows 0 1 submatrix ;
: right ( stereo -- v ) | stereo | stereo 0 stereo n-rows 1 2 submatrix ;
: sine-instrument ( hz instrument -- ) | hz instrument | { } [ { } hz :fixed-hz ! ] :oscillators ! instrument instrument-patch! ;

\ === pitch symbols ===
:a4 pitch>midi . cr                          \ 69
:c4 pitch>midi . cr                          \ 60
:c#4 pitch>midi . :db4 pitch>midi . cr       \ 61 61
:b3 pitch>midi . cr                          \ 59
:bb5 pitch>midi . cr                         \ 82 (b, flat, octave 5)
:c-1 pitch>midi . :g9 pitch>midi . cr        \ 0 127 (the MIDI range)
clear

\ === quarter tones: + raises a quarter tone, d lowers one ===
:c+4 pitch>midi . :ed4 pitch>midi . cr       \ 60.5 63.5
:c#+4 pitch>midi . :ebd4 pitch>midi . cr     \ 61.5 62.5 (three quarters sharp and flat)
:dd4 pitch>midi . :bd4 pitch>midi . cr       \ 61.5 70.5 (after the letter, d is the accidental)
:c+-1 pitch>midi . cr                        \ 0.5 (octave -1 still follows)
:c+4 pitch>hz 1000 * round 1000 / . cr       \ 269.292 (a quarter tone above 261.626)
clear

\ === numbers pass through ===
0 pitch>midi . 127 pitch>midi . 60.5 pitch>midi . cr   \ 0 127 60.5
clear

\ === frequencies ===
:a4 pitch>hz . cr                            \ 440
:a5 pitch>hz . :a3 pitch>hz . cr             \ 880 220
69 pitch>hz . cr                             \ 440
:c4 pitch>hz 1000 * round 1000 / . cr        \ 261.626
clear

\ === render-audio: shape and silence ===
silence-audio 0.5 render-audio dim . . cr              \ 2 24000 (columns, rows)
0 render-audio dim . . cr                        \ 2 0
silence-audio 0.25 render-audio abs max . cr           \ 0 (nothing playing)
{ } 0 instrument-patch! :a4 1 0 note-on 0.1 render-audio abs max 0 > . cr   \ 1
silence-audio 0.1 render-audio abs max . cr            \ 0 (silence-audio ended the note)
clear

\ === consecutive renders continue one signal ===
silence-audio :a4 1 0 note-on 0.5 render-audio to opening 0.5 render-audio to closing
silence-audio :a4 1 0 note-on 1 render-audio to whole
opening closing vstack whole = . cr              \ 1
clear

\ === the same seed renders the same noise ===
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :white } ] } 0 instrument-patch!
: noisy ( -- m ) silence-audio :a4 1 0 note-on 0.1 render-audio ;
3 seed noisy 3 seed noisy = . cr                 \ 1
3 seed noisy 4 seed noisy = . cr                 \ 0
silence-audio clear

\ === two instruments play their own patches ===
silence-audio 1000 0 sine-instrument 1500 1 sine-instrument
:a4 1 0 note-on :a4 1 1 note-on 0.5 render-audio left to both
both 1000 amp . both 1500 amp . cr               \ 0.707 0.707
:a4 1 note-off 1 render-audio drop 0.5 render-audio left to one
one 1000 amp . one 1500 amp . cr                 \ 0.707 0 (only instrument 1 was released)
clear

\ === 32 voices sound together; a 33rd steals ===
{ } 0 instrument-patch! silence-audio
: notes-from ( low high -- ) 2 do k k 1 0 note-on loop ;
60 124 notes-from
1 render-audio left to many-voices
many-voices 60 pitch>hz amp 0.01 > . many-voices 122 pitch>hz amp 0.01 > . cr   \ 1 1 (the lowest and highest of 32)
90 0 note-off 0.1 render-audio drop
123 1 0 note-on 1 render-audio left to stolen
stolen 90 pitch>hz amp . stolen 123 pitch>hz amp 0.01 > . stolen 60 pitch>hz amp 0.01 > . cr   \ 0 1 1 (the released voice was taken)
124 1 0 note-on 1 render-audio left to oldest
oldest 60 pitch>hz amp . oldest 124 pitch>hz amp 0.01 > . cr   \ 0 1 (none released: the oldest was taken)
silence-audio clear

\ === a repeated note-on retriggers the same voice ===
1000 0 sine-instrument :a4 1 0 note-on :a4 1 0 note-on 0.5 render-audio left 1000 amp . cr   \ 0.707 (one voice, not two)
silence-audio clear

\ === :level and velocity ===
{ :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } ] :level 0.5 } 0 instrument-patch! :a4 1 0 note-on 0.5 render-audio left 1000 amp . cr   \ 0.354
silence-audio { :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } ] } 0 instrument-patch! :a4 0.5 0 note-on 0.5 render-audio left 1000 amp . cr     \ 0.354 (full sensitivity)
silence-audio { :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } ] :velocity-sensitivity 0 } 0 instrument-patch! :a4 0.5 0 note-on 0.5 render-audio left 1000 amp . cr   \ 0.707 (velocity ignored)
silence-audio { :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } ] :velocity-sensitivity 0.5 } 0 instrument-patch! :a4 0 0 note-on 0.5 render-audio left 1000 amp . cr   \ 0.354 (half the gain comes from velocity)
silence-audio clear

\ === :pan, constant power ===
{ :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } ] :pan -1 } 0 instrument-patch! :a4 1 0 note-on 0.5 render-audio to hard-left
hard-left left 1000 amp . hard-left right 1000 amp . cr           \ 1 0
silence-audio { :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } ] :pan 1 } 0 instrument-patch! :a4 1 0 note-on 0.5 render-audio to hard-right
hard-right left 1000 amp . hard-right right 1000 amp . cr         \ 0 1
silence-audio { :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } ] :pan 0.5 } 0 instrument-patch! :a4 1 0 note-on 0.5 render-audio to leaning
leaning left 1000 amp . leaning right 1000 amp . cr               \ 0.383 0.924 (cos and sin of 3 pi / 8)
silence-audio clear

\ === :glide: the pitch slides from the instrument's previous note, linearly in semitones ===
: glided ( glide -- stereo ) | glide | silence-audio { } glide :glide ! 0 instrument-patch! :a4 1 0 note-on 0.2 render-audio drop :a5 1 0 note-on 0.3 render-audio left ;
0.1 glided to sliding
sliding 0 2400 0 1 submatrix 880 amp 0.1 < . cr        \ 1 (the first 50 ms are still below 880 Hz)
sliding 5280 14400 0 1 submatrix 880 amp . cr          \ 0.707 (arrived by 0.11 s)
0 glided 480 2400 0 1 submatrix 880 amp . cr           \ 0.707 (:glide 0 jumps, from the end of the 5 ms attack)
silence-audio { :glide 0.1 } 0 instrument-patch! :a5 1 0 note-on 0.1 render-audio left 880 amp . cr   \ 0.707 (a first note after silence-audio does not glide)
silence-audio clear

\ === note-off of a pitch that is not sounding does nothing ===
:c4 0 note-off 0.1 render-audio abs max . cr     \ 0

\ errors
:h4 pitch>midi                                   \ (not a letter a-g)
:c pitch>midi                                    \ (no octave)
:c10 pitch>midi                                  \ (above 127)
:c#-2 pitch>midi                                 \ (below 0)
-1 pitch>midi                                    \ (negative number)
128 pitch>hz                                     \ (above 127)
"c4" pitch>midi                                  \ (a string, not a symbol)
:c++4 pitch>midi                                 \ (two quarter-tone accidentals)
:cd-1 pitch>midi                                 \ (below 0)
:g+9 pitch>midi                                  \ (above 127)
:a4 1.5 0 note-on                                \ (velocity above 1)
:a4 1 16 note-on                                 \ (instrument out of range)
:h4 1 0 note-on                                  \ (not a pitch)
:a4 "one" 0 note-on                              \ (velocity not a float)
:a4 -1 note-off                                  \ (instrument out of range)
-1 render-audio                                  \ (negative)
601 render-audio                                 \ (over 600 s)
"1" render-audio                                 \ (not a float)
